Pinned revision: 81aec25ccbb98f4873a255f7551ac4dadac59b4a
OPN/SSG/ADPCM core subset. See LICENSE.

Local patches:
1. Value-initialize fm_operator::m_cache. Normal synthesis fills it in prepare();
   initialization gives the fields a defined state and addresses cpp:S2107.
2. Add an optional host-owned YM2608 channel-output cache and an accessor to
   the last SSG outputs. When requested, FM/ADPCM voices are rendered individually
   before the same aggregate DAC clamp. The original mixed path remains available.
   No clocks, envelopes, operator calculations or raw core state fields change.
   SSG separation is used only at MAX fidelity, whose prescalers repeat samples.
3. Add explicit YM2608 port peeks, effective register accessors and safe SSG /
   ADPCM external-peek callbacks for debugger use. Normal read/write semantics
   and serialized core fields are unchanged. Hosts/SSG overrides without a
   peek callback return FFh rather than calling a potentially destructive read.
   Contrib/makoto-peek-test.cc checks values against cloned-core real reads and
   proves that peeks leave chip state and host side effects untouched.


4. Add a debugger register-write helper that uses normal port semantics but
   restores the CPU address latch afterward. The host synchronizes audio first.
   Contrib/makoto-register-test.py compares full chip state with equivalent I/O
   writes, including timers, ADPCM RAM and prescalers. No serialized fields change.

Contrib/makoto-core-test.cc compares both paths, including chip state, for
360,000 samples covering all 16 voices and all three prescalers. It also pins a
1133-byte reference state (FNV-1a 4faf7577). This fingerprint is a regression
check, not a security checksum.

Makoto sound-state versions 1 through 4 use this pinned raw YMFM layout.
Version 3 uses native openMSX class versioning; legacy version 2 additionally
stored coreFormat=1, which the compatibility reader validates. Future core
upgrades must bump the sound-state version and retain an appropriate reader
or converter; byte count alone is not a sufficient compatibility check.
Version 4 drops redundant host register/latch copies; legacy copies are ignored
after reading them. Host filter and voice caches are separately serialized.
